          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Directly analogous to the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completion+of+a+ring"} completion of a ring
            is the
            %em completion of a module
            over that ring.
          %p
            In particular the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+completion"} formal completion
            or
            %em adic completion
            of a ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            at an ideal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
            has a corresponding analog for modules. Where the adic completion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi A
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo ∧
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{\mathfrak{a}}^\wedge
            of the ring itself has the geometric interpretation of forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+neighbourhood"} formal neighbourhood
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
